# Dependency direction

`courses → shells → subjects → core`. The checker is `packages/checks/deps.mjs`, and it runs as part of `npm test`.

- Core imports neither `@flux/subjects` nor `@flux/shells` nor anything under `courses/`. A relative path that climbs out of `packages/core` into a subject, a shell, or a course fails the check.
- A subject may import `@flux/core`. A subject imports no shell, no course, and no file under `site/`.
- A shell may import `@flux/core` and `@flux/subjects`. A shell imports no course. A shell names no course and no chapter.
- A course may import `@flux/core`, `@flux/subjects`, and `@flux/shells`. A course imports no other course and no file under `site/`.
- The site may import core, subjects, and courses. It is where the course list lives.
- External packages (`vite`, `katex`, `three`, `node:`) are fine from any layer.

Course-specific rules (TI-84 quartiles, Merino notation, Hibbeler sign conventions, PHY notes structure) live in the course, or in `AGENTS.md` until that course is ported. They are not copied into `packages/core`.
